{"name": "r1102b-B4", "sha256": "a221905a8fa09dbbcd0519b5f84a221c5a31a5b2ad7fef6a7b99abc90d20906b", "words": 175, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.6027544736862183, "fraction_ai_assisted": 4.980111458838415e-22, "fraction_human": 0.39724552631378174, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/ecf802cd-e675-4bf6-9845-87870cddf8b4", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:19:58Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Medium", 29, 0, 178, "Aside from focusing on things in your direct experience, you can also suggest yourself into greater alertness (it's still relaxed-alert, not paranoid-alert). Keep your eyes open."], ["Human Written", "High", 18, 178, 283, " Use a small hand movement each time you make the auto-suggestion that you're gaining increasing clarity."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 12, 283, 342, " Then stop the hand movement and see where your mind is at."], ["Human Written", "Low", 12, 342, 404, " That hand movement is the mental escape into the body's flow."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 18, 404, 512, " Say something like,\n“Starting with your eyes open, press your thumb to your forefinger, gently, and let go."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 30, 512, 659, " Each time you do, you get a little more awake… Press and let go again, a bit clearer. And once more, and now you’re clearer than when you started."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 3, 659, 678, " Now stop pressing."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 22, 678, 809, " In the first second after you stop, is the pressing still echoing somewhere? Start with your fingers, which may still be tingling."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 29, 809, 961, " Next, see if your breath kept the rhythm going. Then check whether your attention is still waiting for the next press. Or maybe there’s no echo at all."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 10, 961, 1017, " Just notice, sit up straight and work from this level.”"]]}
{"name": "r1102b-D1", "sha256": "c776f20cf559fa7c91c097186e543944390888692e8bc68e6d0265b652e1c123", "words": 131, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.3352518081665039, "fraction_ai_assisted": 7.514966933344932e-26, "fraction_human": 0.6647481918334961, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/cebaccad-d951-4faf-8f36-282f80d44271", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:20:03Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 41, 0, 207, "Pattern 10: Meta Model questions — the de-hypnosis tool\nTo 'Milton Model' is to open things up, so the listener can fill in what fits for them. To 'Meta Model' is to stop and ask, \"What do you mean by that?\""], ["Human Written", "Medium", 12, 207, 264, " In order to be ethical with people, you need to do both."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 12, 264, 340, "\nWhen something sounds true but vague, ask: \"What do you mean, specifically?"], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 16, 340, 432, " According to who? Compared to what? Always, or never? What exactly would happen if you did?"], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 12, 432, 497, " How do you know that, and what evidence would change your mind?\""], ["Human Written", "High", 41, 497, 695, "\nSo when someone is starting to tense up in their body, use the Milton Model to help them soften. And when you feel you're losing track of what's really going on, that's the time for the Meta Model."]]}
